WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
i miss you  so much  andy circus and venom literally became  voices inside of tom hardy's ear on set  for venom let there be carnage from  circus imitating venom on set to  orchestrating  650 extras during the rave scene filming  of the second venom movie was seriously  intense then evolves into a physical  altercation carnage grabbing is one of  the most epic scenes and behind the  scenes was no different rigged up with  wires and harnesses all the motions were  mimicked and the actor was spun about in  the air and when it was time for cgi to  work its magic effects took over and  filled in where carnage should be to  help bring the right vibes on set a  large claw was also around to help block  where the cgi would appear  when eddie and venom begin their major  brawl the apartment becomes absolute  chaos with furniture and objects flying  everywhere this was actually all  captured live on set the creative team  had their work cut out for them as they  tied up all the objects that got thrown  which literally flew out of the flew out  of the window with string in order to  achieve the effects we see in the film  as for hardy's stunt double jacob tamori  was rigged up to harnesses and literally  smashed around into furniture andy  circus has so much experience working  with cgi characters and as an actor  himself that he couldn't help but jump  in on occasion and direct tom hardy  while performing hardy's parts himself  getting into the character's head as the  director was an important aspect for  circus because venom's dialogue was  constantly changing so the actor  director duo could riff off each other  and find new lines at this point andy  comes out with some very good  impressions  the team had to make sure they filmed  all the options they might need before  the movie went into the editing stage so  they could have enough material to play  with what didn't make the final cut were  the many sometimes questionable venom  impressions behind the scenes that's  stoic you have a stoic all right mine's  a little bit more  the rave scene in venom let there be  carnage is incredible with all the  lights puppets and action and pulling it  off was a pretty exciting feat  the scene was written into the script  but pretty loosely so director andy  serkis was able to go into filming with  an open mind and play around with the  actors and creative team with a whopping  650 extras on set the energy was high  and definitely helped with the flow of  the sequence immensely the environment  was made to be pretty remarkable with  the giant puppets brought in and  extensive colorful lights it was  definitely easy for the actors to  imagine and perform a major party it was  always going to be a kind of carnival  day of the damned kind of all night of  the damn sort of festival tom hardy gave  his all no matter whether the cameras  were rolling or they were just  rehearsing a scene when he had to  perform his big apartment fight as eddie  brock against venom hardy often  vocalized any injury pretty intensely  he'd literally go up  even though hardy obviously wasn't  battling him in person the actor would  react and make sounds as if he were hit  totally convincing he's been in an  actual fight the voice of venom was  always in tom hardy's head quite  literally since the actor was performing  his scenes opposite venom alone before  getting to set hardy recorded every  single one of the lines and then using  earbuds listened to all of venom's  dialogue as they came and he could  respond in real time this meant the  actor also felt able to improvise  talking over venom and really bringing  magic to the scene with the help of this  sneaky trick hardy was able to  differentiate and really give a life to  both characters in some cases the sound  team would record his lines in the  morning and then when filming play them  back so he could perform that way we  have a feeling these scenes made a lot  more sense for the team watching when it  wasn't just tom hardy hearing venom  andy circus was pretty creative and  hands-on when directing the second venom  film going so far is to become a little  voice in lead actor tom hardy's head  since the actor already had an earpiece  tucked away so he could hear venom's  lines circus would occasionally pop onto  the mic and give him directions live  during the middle of scenes this meant  at any time hardy could suddenly get  blocking directions while performing the  fact that he excelled in this is just a  testament to how gifted a performer he  is  by the time the venom let there be  carnage team finished filming the  apartment battle it looked like a  tornado had come through while they  could have used cgi to show how  destroyed the apartment gets a  combination of the editing and practical  effects were used to help authentically  portray the wild sequence we wanted to  literally physically smash that place up  at one point venom's tongue was played  by a green foam bat and chickens get  thrown about which aren't real chickens  those chickens we see in the kitchen  with eddie brock and venom  those are real  except for the ones that get injured  that is  not to worry no birds were harmed in the  making while it's definitely easier to  manage and handle cgi birds as opposed  to the real thing the team lucked out  with their surprisingly unfussy unmessy  and very professional chickens  the perfect chickens to work with while  tom hardy did perform a ton of his own  stunts and fights in the film he did  have a stunt double who stepped in to  take over when the scene was too  dangerous or could injure hardy in the  process the eddie venom actor was  particularly at risk since he'd had two  knee operations only eight weeks before  filming  this meant jacob tomorry took the reins  when eddie needed to be thrown through a  wall or leaping through windows  before filming even began jacob tamari  would often check in with hardy to see  what his weight was at so he could try  to match the physique when he had to  double him on screen  since he couldn't match hardy's  physicality completely tamari actually  wears what's called a trap suit which is  essentially muscle padding for his  shoulders  let's just say very few people were fans  of woody harrelson's wig in the first  venom  including woody harrelson the red really  was just a strange choice thankfully it  was out with the old and he was given a  new less intensely colored wig that  worked out much better in this film  every detail had to be thought of to  ensure the cgi in the film came across  as realistically as possible when  bringing venom to the screen details  like the colors tom hardy wore made a  big impact in this lighting we can see  that hardy's burnt orange bathrobe looks  quite dark offering the perfect space  for venom to emerge from and so in fact  that affects costume even choices of  costume color without attention being  paid to these seemingly insignificant  details we wouldn't get the incredible  visuals we see in the final cut  when it came to the motorcycle scenes  hardy performed some of the moments but  when the requirements became too risky a  stunt specialist with precision riding  skills took over the speedy scenes  all of this was performed on an upgrade  of what eddie wrote in the first venom  film he's still on a ducati but a ducati  panigale also known as a superbike is  his ride of choice in this movie the  original bike was specifically chosen  for its more rugged look and because of  how it could perform certain stunts  not a detail gets overlooked with this  crew  it's no wonder tom hardy tells the story  as eddie and venom so well since he  actually had a part in writing it this  is the actor's first writing credit and  the whole process definitely helped him  with getting into his character and  understanding how to portray the scenes  so it's just making up stories really  and problem solving venom is a film with  tons of passion humor and special  effects all of which comes together to  bring us yet another fantastic film  about this anti-hero we are seriously  impressed with just how innovative the  creative team was

